output.generality:
Helps GROUP BY on one or more integer keys (dense primary/foreign keys) where min/max stats are known, the range needs between perfect_ht_threshold+1 and 22 bits, and the estimated input is at least half the key range. In those cases hashing and probing become direct array indexing, and the combine and output scan run in parallel.

It does not apply when:
- the key range is sparse or the input estimate is small (the density guard keeps the radix HT);
- there are no stats, or the keys are not integers;
- an aggregate is DISTINCT or has no combine callback;
- the per-thread tables would exceed 1/8 of memory_limit;
- the plan uses grouping sets.

Also, when the key range needs no more bits than perfect_ht_threshold, only the parallel source/combine change applies, and only once the table has at least 2^16 slots (possible only if the user raises the threshold to 16 or more).
